      "latency_ms": 79686.3,
      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1262,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound with the chemical formula **H₂O**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, how it works, and why it is unique:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure and Polarity\nWater is a **polar molecule**. This means the electrons in the water molecule are not shared equally between the oxygen and the hydrogen atoms.\n*   **Oxygen** is more \"electronegative\" (it pulls electrons toward itself) than hydrogen.\n*   This creates a slight negative charge on the oxygen side and a slight positive charge on the hydrogen side.\n*   This polarity is what allows water to stick to itself (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion), and it makes water an excellent solvent for dissolving many other materials.\n\n### 2. The Three States of Matter\nWater is unique because it can exist naturally in all three states of matter on Earth:\n*   **Solid (Ice):** When frozen, water molecules lock into a rigid, crystalline structure.\n*   **Liquid (Water):** The state we are most familiar with, where molecules move freely but stay close together.\n*   **Gas (Steam/Vapor):** When heated, water molecules gain enough energy to fly apart and fill the air.\n\n### 3. Key Physical Properties\nWater has several properties that make it essential for life and the planet:\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Because of its polarity, water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This allows it to transport nutrients and waste within living organisms and in the environment.\n*   **High Specific Heat:** Water requires a lot of energy to heat up and a lot of energy to cool down. This helps regulate the Earth's temperature, preventing drastic fluctuations.\n*   **Density Anomaly:** Unlike most substances, water is **less dense** as a solid (ice) than as a liquid. This is because the hydrogen bonds in ice form a rigid lattice that takes up more space. Because ice floats, it insulates the water below, allowing life to survive under frozen lakes.\n\n### 4. Abundance\nWater is the most abundant molecule on the surface of the Earth. It covers about 71% of the planet and makes up about 60% of the human body. It is found in oceans, rivers, lakes, underground aquifers, and the atmosphere as clouds and vapor."
